In conclusions, we showed that CMs obtained from AF patient-derived iPSCs have significant alterations in two ion currents important for cell automaticity that may represent the substrate for triggering AF. Thus we demonstrated for the first time that iPSC-CMs represent a suitable in vitro model to study AF with complex genetic background.
