Background: Previous studies have suggested a role for the neuronal sodium channel Nav1.8 (encoded by SCN10A) in cardiac conduction and late sodium current magnitude. Nav1.8 is highly expressed in dorsal root ganglia and plays a role in pain perception, but its presence and functional relevance in cardiomyocytes is debated.
