Background: Endothelial progenitor cells $(\mathsf{E P C s})$ are a type of stem cells present in the peripheral blood with role in the maintenance of vascular endothelium integrity. Normal EPC function can be preserved by certain microRNAs (miRNAs), but little is known about EPC dysfunctionality in atherosclerosis.
