Background: Electrical vagal nerve stimulation (VNS) protects from myocardial and vascular injury following cardiac ischemia/reperfusion (IR) via a mechanism involving activation of alpha-7 nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (a7 nAChRs) and reduced inflammation. Arginase has been proposed to be involved in development of IR injury and endothelial dysfunction after induction by pro-inflammatory mediators.
