Then we engineered poly (lactic-co-glycolic acid) nanoparticle containing cyclosporine A (CsA-NP) that inhibits mPTP opening and pitavastatin (Pit-NP) that reduces monocyte-mediated inflammation. In CypD-KO mice, Pit-NP reduced the recruitment of Ly6Chigh inflammatory monocytes and infarct size, whereas CsA-NP reduced infarct size in CCR2-KO mice. Simultaneous treatment with CsA-NP and Pit-NP at the time of reperfusion presented a remarkable reduction in infarct size after IR injury with 30 or 60 min of ischemia(Fig.B).
