Methods: Isolated Langendorff perfused rat hearts were subjected to either IPC ( $3\times5\min$ global ischaemia-reperfusion) or sham. Effluent was collected and perfused through a naı¨ve-isolated heart for $10-m i n$ prior to a $35-m i n$ regional ischaemia and $60-\mathsf{m i n}$ reperfusion. The ganglionic antagonist hexamethonium $(50\upmu\mathsf{M})$ and nitric oxide synthase (NOS) blocker L-NAME $100\upmu\up M)$ were used to investigate the mechanism of effluent-mediated cardioprotection. Finally, the concentration of acetylcholine in effluent from isolated rat hearts was measured before and immediately after the IPC protocol.
