Background: Ischemic preconditioning (IPreC) is a powerful intervention to reduce myocardial ischemic injury in all species studied including human beings. The aim of this study was to investigate whether the protection afforded by IPreC of the human myocardium: (i) is a common phenomenon, and (ii) is influenced by cardiac and systemic clinical conditions and medical treatments.
