Purpose: Pressure overload LV hypertrophy and its reversion are complex biological phenomena that appear in the natural and treated histories of very prevalent cardiovascular diseases. Several animal models mimic the clinical scenario and most popular is the constriction of the aortic arch in mice according to Rockma´ns technique (RT). RT is highly operator-dependent, technically demanding, poorly reproducible, and traumatic for the aorta. We devised a novel technique that provides individualized, fully controlled, reproducible and technically easier constriction of the mid aortic arch with no need for even transient aortic occlusion.
