Background: HMGB1 is a nuclear factor that when secreted, is able to signal tissue damage. HMGB1 is also implicated in cardiac regeneration and remodeling after myocardial infarction (MI). The extracellular HMGB1 activity depends on its redox state: the fully-reduced-HMGB1 has chemotactic effect while the disulfide-HMGB1 induces cytokines expression.
