Background: We recently showed that in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (HCM), genotype is not predictive of onset or severity of atrial myopathy, which rather appears to be driven by hemodynamic determinants, such as diastolic dysfunction and outflow obstruction (Bongini et al. Am J Cardiol 2016). In human and murine HCM ventricular myocardium, primary changes in myofilament function, related to the presence of disease-causing mutations in sarcomeric proteins, are often associated with secondary abnormalities due to adverse remodeling of cardiomyocyte EC-coupling (Coppini et al. Circulation 2013).
