Introduction: Mutations mainly in sarcomeric and Z-disc proteins including cysteine and glycine-rich protein 3 (CSRP3) have been shown to cause hypertrophic (HCM) and dilated cardiomyopathies (DCM). However, the underlying molecular mechanisms remain not well understood.
